      "textEn": "526\n\nSupreme—extreme; Arhat—valuable; Mani-vrata—many jewels; Kirit—crown; Katak—bangles; Angadaih—with bangles;\nBhrajamanam—radiant; Padma—lotus; Karam—in hand; Shankha—conch; Chakra—wheel; Gada—and mace; Dharam—held;\nSrivatsa—Srivatsa symbol; Vakshasam—on the chest; Bhrajat—adorned; Kaustubham—with the Kaustubha gem; Van-mala—with flowers\nA garland is worn. Adorned with a crown, bracelets, and armlets studded with many precious jewels, and wearing a dhoti,\nwearing a sacred thread, a necklace around the neck, anklets, and earrings, the Lord was radiant with splendor. They had a\nlotus flower in one hand and others held conch, chakra and mace. On his\nchest was the Srivatsa symbol, a radiant Kaustubha jewel, and a garland of flowers adorned. By the Sun-born, by the chiefs, by the assembly. Suresha, Brahma, Rudra, and the nine great Brahmins. 53. Prahradanaradavasu mukhyairbhagavato tatamaih.\nHe who is praised by his own self, by his own good words. 54>. Shriya, nourished, ear, conqueror, fame, fame, victory. By knowledge, by knowledge, by power, and by Maya. 55 Meaning of the word\n\nSunand-nand-pramukhaih—Sunand, Nand, etc.; Parshadhaih—with their associates; Sanak-adibhih—Sanak Kumar and their brothers; Sahit—with; Sur-ishaish—from the main deities; Brahma-Rudra-adi-ahyah—from Brahma, Rudra, etc.; Navabhih—nine; Cha—and; Dwija-uttamaih—from the chief\nBrahmins (Marichi, etc.); Prahlad-Narada-Vasu-pramukhaih—Prahlad, Narad, From the upper Vasu etc.; by the best of devotees; praised; by different emotions each; by words; pure; done; by Shriya, Pushti, Gira, Kantya, Kirti, Tushti, Ilahi, Urjaya—Shri, nourishment, Gira, radiance, fame, fame, satisfaction, Ilahi, energy, named inner powers\nFrom the powers; by knowledge and ignorance—from the powers named knowledge and ignorance; by Shakti—by one's delightful power; by Maya—by one's\nFrom the creative power; with; and; having been served. Among those who worshiped by surrounding God, Nand, Sunan