      "textEn": "534\n\nSarvatmane, Sarvadhiyane, and Sakshine. This flow of qualities is caused by ignorance.\nIt prevails in the world of gods and humans. 12. Meaning of the word\n\nTubhyam—to you; Namah—obeisance; Te—yours; Tu—so; Avisakta—separate, detached; Drishtaye—with the seer; Sarva-atmane—of all souls; Sarva—everything; Dhayam—of consciousness; Cha—and; Sakshine—to the witness; Guna—of qualities; Pravahah—stream;\nAyam—this; Avidyaya—due to ignorance; Krutah—produced; Pravartate—continues; Deva—as gods; Nri—as humans;\nTiryak—as animals; Atmasu—of those whose form is in them. I greet you, who, being the supreme form of all beings, with impartiality, every\none's consciousness is witness. The flow of your physical qualities born of ignorance flows among those beings\nwith strength, who take the form of gods, humans, and animals. Agnirmukham te avanirangirikshanam\nSuryo nabho nabhiratho dishah shrutih.\n\nGutaang, Jananendriya; Tu—Tatha; Vrishti—Varsha; Tava—Tumhaara; Veeryam—Veerya; Ishyate—Mana jaata hai. Fire is said to be your mouth, the earth is your feet, the sun is your eye, and\nthe sky is your navel. Directions are your auditory senses, the main deities are your arms, and\nthe ocean is your stomach. Heaven is considered your head, and air is your life-air and\nphysical strength. Trees and herbs are the hair of your body, clouds are the hair of your head.\nAnd mountains are your bones and nails. The passing of day and night is your eyelids\nThe blinking is, Prajapati is your genitals and rain is your semen."
