      "textEn": "535\n\nThrough the self-existent being, the projected\nworlds are many, living beings are numerous. As the water is pleased by the water-lily,\nAnd also by the musk-camphor. 15. Meaning of the word\n\nTvayi—within you; Avyaya-Atman—indestructible; Purusha—God; Vipakshitaah—produced; Lokah—world; Sa-palaah—\nCaring deities including; Bahu—many; Jiva—with living beings; Sankulaah—gathered; Yatha—as; Jale—in water;\nSanjihite—they wander here and there; Jala-Okasah—animals of the water; Api—indeed; Udumbara—in the Gular fruit (Gular); Va—\nOr; Mashakah—small insects; Manah—mind (and other senses); Maye—within you..\n\nYour respective presiding deities and countless beings, along with the entire world, are emanated from the Supreme Immortal.\nThey are born. All these worlds, mind, and senses, based on that, keep revolving within you, which\nJust as aquatic creatures swim in the ocean, or small insects keep piercing inside the gular fruit. Yaani yaaniha rupani kreeednartham bibhharshi hi.\nThose who are not born of the earth sing of your glory. 16. Meaning of the word\n\nThat is, that is—who, who; Iha—in this world; Rupani—forms; Kridan—in play; Artham—purpose; Bibharshi—expressing; Hi—\nUndoubtedly; Tahi—by them; Amrusha—washed; Shuchah—of their sorrows; Lokah—people; Muda—joyfully; Gayanti—singing\nare; Te—yours; Yashah—glory. To enjoy your divine plays, you manifest yourself in various forms in this material world,\nand these incarnations wash away all the sorrows of those people who joyfully sing your\nglory. Salutations to the one who is the cause of the destruction of the delusion. Salutations to you, O Lord, who are the destroyer of the demon Madhu and the nectar of the nectar of the earth. 17). A-ku-para-yah, Brihatte Namo, Mandaradharine.\nSalutations to the one who is the destroyer of enemies, the embodiment of the boar. 18>. Meaning of the word\n\nNamah—Greetings; Karan—The original cause of creation; Matsyaya—The manifestation of God in the f